# Sales Commission Plan — FY26: quota relief

> Module QuotaRelief

> Using Commission

This module computes the Quota against which Attainment is measured, after
relief for qualifying absence under S-6. The *data* flows relief-first: S-6.2
says relief is applied before Attainment is calculated, so the relieved Quota is
an input to `Commission.Attainment` and never a correction applied to a figure
computed from the assigned Quota.

The *module* dependency runs the other way, which is deliberate. S-6.1 has to
know the Plan Year, and S-1.1 — which is the only place the Plan Year window is
stated — is encoded in `Commission`; restating the window here would be a second
copy of a clause that exists once. `CommissionAfterRelief` below then composes
the whole chain in the order S-6.2 fixes. Nothing in `Commission` imports this
module, so there is no cycle.

Nothing here is a judgement input. The three absence categories S-6.1 names are
legal statuses payroll records, and the 30-day continuous-period threshold is
what supplies the content of "long-term" — the Plan does not leave that to an
assessor.

## Prologue — declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration AbsenceCategory:
  -- StatutoryParentalLeave
  -- AdoptionLeave
  -- LongTermSicknessAbsence
  -- OtherAbsence

# One continuous absence, inclusive of both endpoints: an absence recorded as
# starting and ending on the same day is one day of absence.
declaration structure AbsencePeriod:
  data category content AbsenceCategory
  data start_date content date
  data end_date content date

declaration scope QualifyingAbsence:
  input absence content AbsencePeriod
  output days_of_absence content integer
  output is_qualifying_category content boolean
  output is_qualifying content boolean
  output in_year_days_of_absence content integer

declaration scope RelievedQuota:
  input annual_quota content money
  input absence_periods content list of AbsencePeriod
  internal qualifying_absences content list of AbsencePeriod
  output relief_days content integer
  output relief content money
  output relieved_quota content money
  output quota_for_attainment content money

declaration scope CommissionAfterRelief:
  input assigned_quota content money
  input absence_periods content list of AbsencePeriod
  input net_booked_revenue content money
  input new_logo_share content decimal
  input commencement_date content date
  input annual_base_salary content money
  output quota_relief scope RelievedQuota
  output commission scope Commission.CommissionPayable
  output quota_for_attainment content money
  output commission_payable content money
```

## S-6 Quota relief — the gateway

| COMM-PLAN S-6.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:83)
|
| Where an Employee is absent on statutory parental leave, adoption leave
| or long-term sickness absence for a continuous period of 30 days or more, the
| Employee's Quota is reduced by 1/365th of the annual Quota for each day of such
| absence.

S-6.1 asks two questions and the whole of this module's correctness depends on
keeping them apart. The **gateway** question is whether the Employee "is absent
... for a continuous period of 30 days or more". It is asked of a recorded
absence as a whole: the test applies to each absence separately, so two
unconnected 20-day absences do not combine, and "30 days or more" is inclusive,
so a 30-day absence qualifies and a 29-day one does not. The **quantum**
question — by how much the Quota falls — is answered separately below.

Days are counted inclusively of both endpoints, which is the ordinary reading
of an absence "from" one date "to" another: 1 January to 30 January is 30 days.
`days_of_absence` is the length of the whole continuous absence, wherever its
days fall, because that is what the gateway is measured on.

```catala
scope QualifyingAbsence:
  definition days_of_absence equals
    integer of ((absence.end_date - absence.start_date) / (1 day)) + 1

  definition is_qualifying_category equals
    absence.category with pattern StatutoryParentalLeave
    or absence.category with pattern AdoptionLeave
    or absence.category with pattern LongTermSicknessAbsence

  definition is_qualifying equals
    is_qualifying_category and days_of_absence >= 30
```

## S-6.1 Which days can be relieved — the Plan Year confines them

| COMM-PLAN S-6.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:83)
|
| Where an Employee is absent on statutory parental leave, adoption leave
| or long-term sickness absence for a continuous period of 30 days or more, the
| Employee's Quota is reduced by 1/365th of the annual Quota for each day of such
| absence.

The days S-6.1 can relieve are days of the Plan Year, and only those. S-1.1
confines the whole Plan to the financial year 1 October 2025 to 30 September
2026; S-2.1 makes the Quota the annual target assigned for that Plan Year; and
S-6.1's unit of relief — 1/365th of the annual Quota — is a proration of that
same 365-day year, there being no other 365-day period in the instrument for the
fraction to refer to. A day that is not a day of the Plan Year therefore has no
1/365th of this Quota to consume. An absence lying wholly in another financial
year relieves nothing (CE-0012), and an absence straddling the boundary passes
the gateway on its full continuous length while relieving only its in-year days
(CE-0013) — the two questions of the clause, answered separately.

`in_year_days_of_absence` is this record's days clipped to the Plan Year window,
which is imported from `Commission` rather than restated. It is not itself a
quantum of relief: overlapping records would each count the shared days, which
is what S-6.1 forbids and what `RelievedQuota` below is careful not to do.

```catala
scope QualifyingAbsence:
  definition in_year_days_of_absence equals
    let first_day equals
      Date.max of absence.start_date, Commission.plan_year_start
    in
    let last_day equals
      Date.min of absence.end_date, Commission.plan_year_end
    in
    if last_day < first_day then 0
    else integer of ((last_day - first_day) / (1 day)) + 1
```

## S-6.1 The quantum — one day, one 1/365th

| COMM-PLAN S-6.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:83)
|
| Where an Employee is absent on statutory parental leave, adoption leave
| or long-term sickness absence for a continuous period of 30 days or more, the
| Employee's Quota is reduced by 1/365th of the annual Quota for each day of such
| absence.

The unit of account in the quantum limb is the **day of absence**, not the
absence record. A day on which the Employee was absent is one day of absence
however many leave categories the HR system records against it, so it attracts
one 1/365th reduction and no more. Summing record lengths double-counts the days
two overlapping records share (CE-0014) and, worse, lets relief exceed 365/365ths
and drive the Quota negative — an outcome no reduction "by 1/365th ... for each
day" of a 365-day year can ever produce.

`relief_days` is therefore the number of days **of the Plan Year** that fall
within some qualifying absence. Catala has no set type, and the two ways to take
a union of date ranges are to merge the ranges or to count the days; this module
counts the days, for three reasons. It is the clause's own unit: "for each day of
such absence" is a predicate over days, and `plan_year_days` is exactly the
domain the 1/365th fraction prorates. It needs no machinery the clause does not
mention, where merging would require a sort, an adjacency rule and a clipping
rule — three inventions the Plan could not adjudicate between. And it makes both
invariants structural rather than argued: a day is counted once because it is one
day, and the count cannot exceed the days of the window.

```catala
# Every day of the Plan Year, from S-1.1's window, which is inclusive at both
# ends and so spans (end - start) + 1 days. `List.sequence` stops one short of
# its second argument, so the day count is itself that argument. Deriving the
# list from the window keeps it from drifting from S-1.1.
declaration plan_year_days content list of date equals
  let days_in_plan_year equals
    integer of
      ((Commission.plan_year_end - Commission.plan_year_start) / (1 day)) + 1
  in
  map each i among (List.sequence of 0, days_in_plan_year)
  to Commission.plan_year_start + i * (1 day)

scope RelievedQuota:
  definition qualifying_absences equals
    list of a among absence_periods
    such that (output of QualifyingAbsence with { -- absence: a }).is_qualifying

  definition relief_days equals
    number of (list of d among plan_year_days
               such that (exists a among qualifying_absences
                          such that a.start_date <= d and d <= a.end_date))
```

## S-6.1 The reduction, and the ceiling the clause implies

| COMM-PLAN S-6.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:83)
|
| Where an Employee is absent on statutory parental leave, adoption leave
| or long-term sickness absence for a continuous period of 30 days or more, the
| Employee's Quota is reduced by 1/365th of the annual Quota for each day of such
| absence.

The reduction itself is the arithmetic the clause states: 1/365th of the annual
Quota per relieved day. The assertions record what the day-counting above makes
true — the window is the 365-day period the 1/365th unit presupposes, and no day
can be counted twice — so relief can never exceed the annual Quota and the
relieved Quota can never go negative, an outcome the clause cannot produce.

```catala
scope RelievedQuota:
  definition relief equals
    annual_quota * (decimal of relief_days / 365.0)

  definition relieved_quota equals
    annual_quota - relief

  assertion number of plan_year_days = 365
  assertion relief_days <= 365
```

## S-6.2 Relief is applied before Attainment is calculated

| COMM-PLAN S-6.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:88)
|
| Quota relief under S-6.1 is applied before Attainment is calculated.

S-6.2 is an ordering rule with a concrete consequence: the denominator of the
S-2.2 quotient is the relieved Quota, not the assigned Quota. That consequence
is carried across the module boundary by naming the quantity —
`quota_for_attainment` is what `Commission.Attainment`'s `quota` input is fed
from, and a caller that passed `annual_quota` instead would be computing a
different and lower Attainment, a different accelerator under S-4 and, because
S-5.2 puts the cap last, a different capped figure too. The identity is the
whole of the clause: S-6.2 adds no arithmetic of its own, it fixes which
arithmetic comes first.

```catala
scope RelievedQuota:
  definition quota_for_attainment equals relieved_quota
```

| COMM-PLAN S-6.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:88)
|
| Quota relief under S-6.1 is applied before Attainment is calculated.

Naming the quantity is not enough, and the adversarial reviewer was right that
it was all this module did. `Commission.CommissionPayable` takes `quota` as a
free input, so until now whether S-6.2 was honoured depended on the caller
remembering to pass `quota_for_attainment` rather than the assigned figure — and
no probe could tell the two apart, because both are just a `money` input. On an
assigned Quota of $1,000,000 with 73 qualifying absence days and Net Booked
Revenue of $800,000 the difference is the whole of an S-4.1 band: 100% Attainment
and an accelerator of 1.5 giving $96,000, against 80% and 1.0 giving $64,000.

`CommissionAfterRelief` closes that gap structurally. It takes the *assigned*
Quota and the absence records, and there is no path through it that reaches
`Commission.CommissionPayable` without passing through `RelievedQuota` first:
the sub-scope's `quota` input is defined here, once, as the relieved figure, and
`absence_periods` is a required input that cannot be defaulted away — an
Employee with no absence is stated as the empty list, affirmatively, rather than
by omission. The ordering S-6.2 mandates is therefore a fact about the code
rather than a convention in the prose. Nothing else is re-encoded: S-2.2, S-3.1,
S-4 and S-5 keep their single encoding in `Commission`, and this scope only
wires them up in the mandated order.

```catala
scope CommissionAfterRelief:
  definition quota_relief.annual_quota equals assigned_quota
  definition quota_relief.absence_periods equals absence_periods

  definition quota_for_attainment equals quota_relief.quota_for_attainment

  definition commission.quota equals quota_relief.quota_for_attainment
  definition commission.net_booked_revenue equals net_booked_revenue
  definition commission.new_logo_share equals new_logo_share
  definition commission.commencement_date equals commencement_date
  definition commission.annual_base_salary equals annual_base_salary

  definition commission_payable equals commission.commission_payable
```
